chunks.representation:
For a constant heating rate:

- flat length $\propto mL$ → longer flat = more latent heat (or more mass);
- slope $\propto 1/(mc)$ → steeper slope = smaller $c$ (or smaller mass);
- plateau height = the melting or boiling temperature.

Cooling curve = mirror image of the heating curve:

- slopes go **down** instead of up;
- flats are at the **same temperatures**;
- energy is **released** ($Q = mL$) at each flat and ($Q = mc\,\Delta T$) on each slope.
